OL,3,CGerry Kelly was 'voice of sanity
OL,4,Cduring insane times', funeral hears
OL,6,FBroadcasting veteran Gerry Kelly was
OL,7,F"the voice of sanity during insane
OL,8,Ftimes" and a "real legend who will
OL,9,Fnever die", his funeral has heard.
OL,11,FThe former UTV and BBC Radio Ulster
OL,12,Fpresenter conducted many high-profile
OL,13,Finterviews, including with an eight-
OL,14,Fyear-old Rory McIlroy as the young
OL,15,Fgolfer chipped balls into a washing
OL,16,Fmachine.
OL,18,FKelly was installed in the Royal
OL,19,FTelevision Society Hall of Fame in
OL,20,F1998 in recognition of his
OL,21,Fcontribution to broadcasting.
OL,26,@oD@AOUpD@FO]pD@NOUqD@JO]
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G1/9
